{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>I have not eaten of it in my mourning.</b> For a mourner is forbidden from sacred gifts. <br><b>And I have not removed any of it while impure.</b> That I did not separate it in a state of impurity. <br><b>And I have not given any of it to the dead</b> — that I did not purchase with it a coffin or shrouds. And the sense is that one need not say for a matter of permission, but even for a matter of mitzvah that involves honor to the living and the dead I did not give of it — meaning that one should not be as one repaying his obligation with it for a mitzvah, and all the more so I did not expend of it for life's needs, but only to eat and drink. <br><b>I have hearkened to the voice of YHWH my Elohim.</b> When I brought it to the chosen house. <br><b>I have done according to all that You have commanded me</b> — that I rejoiced and caused others to rejoice, as it is said: ושמחת בכל הטוב."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:51:15.088664919Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}